    {
      "type": "caption",
      "t": 25.0,
      "dur": 7.5,
      "text": "The plan was to cut Bengal in two, between India and Pakistan."
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "t": 34.0,
      "dur": 7.5,
      "text": "The job of drawing the line went to Cyril Radcliffe, a British lawyer who had never worked in India before."
    },
    {
      "type": "line",
      "name": "radcliffe",
      "t": 42.0,
      "dur": 18.0
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "t": 43.0,
      "dur": 7.5,
      "text": "He had only a few weeks. His line ran through farms, villages and rivers."
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "t": 51.5,
      "dur": 8.0,
      "text": "The main idea was to follow religious majorities, but communities lived mixed together in many places."
    },
